{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"node --input-type=module <<'JS'\nimport {createWorld,step,planShot,health,COURTS,validateCourt} from './src/sim.js';\nfor(let court=0;court<5;court++){\nconst w=createWorld({court,ai:[{style:'mason',perfect:true,reaction:.2},{style:'adaptive',reaction:1,error:.02}]});\nconsole.log(COURTS[court].name,validateCourt({version:1,layout:COURTS[court].layout}),planShot(w,0));\nwhile(w.phase==='play')step(w);\nconsole.log(w.time,w.outcome,health(w,0),health(w,1),w.stats);\n}\nJS\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"node --input-type=module <<'JS'\nimport {createWorld,step,planShot,health,COURTS,validateCourt} from './src/sim.js';\nfor(let court=0;court<5;court++){\nconst w=createWorld({court,ai:[{style:'mason',perfect:true,reaction:.2},{style:'adaptive',reaction:1,error:.02}]});\nconsole.log(COURTS[court].name,validateCourt({version:1,layout:COURTS[court].layout}),planShot(w,0));\nwhile(w.phase==='play')step(w);\nconsole.log(w.time,w.outcome,health(w,0),health(w,1),w.stats);\n}\nJS\"","aggregated_output":"Village Exhibition { valid: true, errors: [] } {\n  power: 0.6583333333333333,\n  type: 1,\n  value: 10.458567980691875,\n  target: 'block'\n}\n15.475 {\n  winner: 0,\n  reason: 'demolition',\n  scores: [ 9, 13 ],\n  banked: [ 9, 0 ]\n} 0.375 0 {\n  shots: [ 6, 6 ],\n  used: [ [ 1 ], [ 2, 1 ] ],\n  collapses: 11,\n  crew: 1,\n  launcher: 0,\n  recoveries: 1,\n  damage: 13,\n  cancels: 0\n}\nQuarry Meet { valid: true, errors: [] } {\n  power: 0.6856666666666666,\n  type: 1,\n  value: 8.3668543845535,\n  target: 'block'\n}\n24.9 {\n  winner: 0,\n  reason: 'demolition',\n  scores: [ 24, 32 ],\n  banked: [ 24, 0 ]\n} 0.075 0 {\n  shots: [ 9, 10 ],\n  used: [ [ 1 ], [ 2, 1 ] ],\n  collapses: 12,\n  crew: 2,\n  launcher: 0,\n  recoveries: 1,\n  damage: 36.400000000000006,\n  cancels: 0\n}\nHigh Keep { valid: true, errors: [] } {\n  power: 0.6583333333333333,\n  type: 1,\n  value: 12.550281576830251,\n  target: 'block'\n}\n15.466666666666667 {\n  winner: 0,\n  reason: 'demolition',\n  scores: [ 9, 13 ],\n  banked: [ 9, 0 ]\n} 0.44680851063829785 0 {\n  shots: [ 6, 6 ],\n  used: [ [ 1 ], [ 2, 1 ] ],\n  collapses: 16,\n  crew: 1,\n  launcher: 0,\n  recoveries: 1,\n  damage: 13,\n  cancels: 0\n}\nLakeside Night Court { valid: true, errors: [] } {\n  power: 0.6583333333333333,\n  type: 1,\n  value: 12.550281576830251,\n  target: 'block'\n}\n20.025 {\n  winner: 1,\n  reason: 'demolition',\n  scores: [ 15, 22 ],\n  banked: [ 0, 22 ]\n} 0 0.04186046511627906 {\n  shots: [ 8, 8 ],\n  used: [ [ 1 ], [ 2, 1 ] ],\n  collapses: 17,\n  crew: 1,\n  launcher: 0,\n  recoveries: 1,\n  damage: 26.000000000000004,\n  cancels: 0\n}\nRoyal Final { valid: true, errors: [] } {\n  power: 0.6719999999999999,\n  type: 1,\n  value: 10.458567980691875,\n  target: 'block'\n}\n24.933333333333334 {\n  winner: 0,\n  reason: 'demolition',\n  scores: [ 24, 25 ],\n  banked: [ 24, 0 ]\n} 0.2 0 {\n  shots: [ 10, 10 ],\n  used: [ [ 1 ], [ 2, 1 ] ],\n  collapses: 16,\n  crew: 1,\n  launcher: 0,\n  recoveries: 1,\n  damage: 36.400000000000006,\n  cancels: 0\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'live:|live\\\\b|tv:|Shell\\\\(|menu:|glyphs|musicVolume|volumeMusic' vendor/engine/API.md | head -n 60 && sed -n '240,310p' vendor/engine/API.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'live:|live\\\\b|tv:|Shell\\\\(|menu:|glyphs|musicVolume|volumeMusic' vendor/engine/API.md | head -n 60 && sed -n '240,310p' vendor/engine/API.md\"","aggregated_output":"51:10. **Faces in dialog**: `talk.say(lines, { name: 'MIRA', portrait: miraRig })` puts a live close-up of that Humanoid (blinking, hair, hat) beside every line. `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 40)` draws one [... omitted end of long line]\n135:- Adjust: `new E.Game({ menu: { items: [['Restart', fn]], settings: [{ key: 'hints', label: 'Hints', value: true }, { key: 'difficulty', options: ['Easy', 'Normal', 'Hard'], value: 'Normal' }], contro [... omitted end of long line]\n136:- Save slots (`game.saves`): three slots and an autosave, each with its place, level and time played. `game.saves.write = () => ({ data, place, level })` and `read = save => {...}`; then `save(slot)`  [... omitted end of long line]\n137:- Prompts: `game.input.label('jump')` is that action's key or button on the player's device, after rebinding ('Space', 'A', '✕'). PlayStation symbols by default: `settings: [{ key: 'glyphs', value: 'p [... omitted end of long line]\n156:- X-ray: `r.actor(..., { xray: true })` shows the actor's hidden part, a translucent tint with a 1-px outline (a checker in `E.style.trans = 'dither'`), wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest [... omitted end of long line]\n164:- Dialog: `const talk = new E.Dialog(game)`; `talk.say(['Line one.', 'Page two.'], { name: 'ELDER', portrait: elderRig, onDone, choices: ['YES', 'NO'], onChoice(i) })` (choices show on the last page:  [... omitted end of long line]\n166:- HTML screens and HUD: `const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: { scale: 2 } (a TV; or `tv: true`), settings, screens: { pause, help, dev: { rows: ['glyphs'] } } })`; `ui.show('title' | 'results' | 'ma [... omitted end of long line]\n171:- Music: `music('title' | 'adventure' | 'dungeon' | 'boss' | 'victory')` (built in; any other name warns and plays nothing), or your own `{ bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [{ wave: 'square', vol: .15, not [... omitted end of long line]\n| Golden-age arcade (Pac-Man, Galaga, Asteroids) | `overhead` (one fixed screen, cabinet art on the sides) | `E.Arcade` (score, lives, extra lives, turns, initials, tables, attract mode); a maze of `E.GridMover`s; moths on `E.Path`s turned by `rot`; `E.wrap` and `wrap: [w, h]` | ARCADE |\n| Twin-stick / run-and-gun (Smash TV, Contra) | `topdown` / `side` | Body or Platformer, Bullets, `weapon: 'gun'`, `point: true` | SHOOTER + ADVENTURE |\n| JRPG (Dragon Quest, Final Fantasy, EarthBound) | `threequarter` town, `brawler` battles | TileMap towns and a big world map, the story and rpg modules, Dialog with markup, `game.saves` slots | RPG |\n| Puzzle (Tetris, Dr. Mario, Puyo, Columns) | `side` (a field in screen pixels) | a cell array, a bag from `E.rng`, `input.repeat` (auto-shift), `grid.groups` (chains), `input.drag()` and `clicked()` for touch; versus: two fields, rows sent across (`game.players`) | PUZZLE |\n| Roguelike (Rogue, Mystery Dungeon, Shiren) | `threequarter` / `iso` | `E.gen` floors, a TileMap of its rows, `E.Grid.from(map)` paths and `fov`, `E.Fog`, `E.Turns` by speed, `game.tween` steps | ROGUELIKE |\n| Tactics (Final Fantasy Tactics, Tactics Ogre, Fire Emblem) | `iso`, turned a quarter | TileMap of block heights, `map.pick` under the cursor, `E.Grid.from(map, { tops: true })` reach over heights, `grid.shape`, `grid.side`, `grid.threat`, `E.Turns` charge time, `E.Story` | TACTICS |\n| Real-time strategy (Warcraft II, StarCraft, Dune II) | `iso` | `E.Strategy` (the strategy module): kinds as data, selection by click, box and group, orders, gold, building, training, fog, an AI's build order and waves; `cam.free`, `{ pick: unit }` and `r.pick`, buildings as `E.SHAPES`, E.Shell's minimap; bodies drawn `every: 3` | RTS |\n| Theme park or city sim (Theme Park, RollerCoaster Tycoon, SimCity) | `iso` | paths as floor tags walked on an `E.Grid`, agents with `E.needs` picking by `E.choose`, `E.Clock` days and light, `game.timeScale` 0 to 4, `E.overlay`, `E.tooltip`; rides as shapes stepped through angles (`params`, `facing`) | SIM |\n| 3D platformer or adventure remake (Mario 64, Ocarina, Crash) | `iso` / `threequarter` / `brawler` | TileMap blocks of different heights + Body `jump()` (z is real height); in real 3D: `E.World3D` (the 3D engine's manual), `camera.lock` | ADVENTURE; 3D ACTION, 3D PLATFORMER |\n| Survival horror (Resident Evil, Alone in the Dark) | the 3D engine's `'zones'` camera | `camera.zones` (fixed cameras by room), `camera.steer` (tank controls), `camera.lock` to aim, `world.through` doors, `world.flashlight`, fog; `E.RPG` inventory, `game.saves` | 3D HORROR |\n| First-person dungeon (Wizardry, Dungeon Master, Eye of the Beholder) | the 3D engine's `'fixed'` camera at the party's eyes | cells of 2 x 2 tiles stepped and turned a quarter at a time (tweened), `E.Grid` paths for the monsters, `E.Turns` `'atb'` (real time) or `'speed'` (turns), `E.Fog` for the automap, `world.thing('door')` gates and `world.unlock`, `rig.drawPortrait` for the party | 3D CRAWLER |\n| Rhythm (Dance Dance Revolution, PaRappa, Beatmania, Space Channel 5) | any (a highway on the overlay) | `E.Rhythm` (the rhythm module): a chart of lane strings in parts on a song's steps, judged in ms of the music clock, combo, life, grade, holds, calls a teacher plays and you answer, `rh.draw` (`arrows: true`); the songbook's songs (`E.Songbook`); lanes as `input.zones` on a phone; `audio.onBeat` moves the dancer | RHYTHM |\n| Sports (Sensible Soccer, NBA Jam) | `threequarter` / `topdown` | the ball an `E.Body` (`bounce`; curl: turn its velocity across its path), passes led to the teammate, `E.arc` for a lob, a shot's meter, formations by where the ball is, `game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })` | SPORTS |\n| Third-person stealth (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear, Tenchu) | `iso` / `threequarter` | TileMap roofs, Mover, `E.sees`, `E.Suspicion`, FlowField `jump` | STEALTH |\n| Kart racing (Super Mario Kart, F-Zero) | Mode 7 (the mode7 module, over any view) | `E.Mode7` over a TileMap track (floor tags: grass, sand, boost), `E.Car` karts (`kart: true`: hop, drift, boost) in an `E.Race` round an `E.Path` (laps, checkpoints, drivers, items), rigs in karts as billboards, `game.splitScreen(2)` for two | KART |\n| 3D kart racing (Mario Kart 64, Crash Team Racing) | the 3D engine's `'behind'` camera | `world.track` (banked, walls, pads, `gaps` for a shortcut), `world.vehicle` karts raced by `E.Race`, split screen through `world.cameras` | 3D RACING |\n| Rail shooters (Star Fox 64, Panzer Dragoon) | the 3D engine's `'behind'` camera | `world.flyer` on rails or free in bounds, rolls (`f.rolling`) turn shots aside, `f.seek` for a charged lock, `Dialog`'s radio | 3D FLIGHT |\n| Road racing (OutRun, Pole Position, Road Rash) | the pseudo-3D road (the road module) | `E.Road` segments (curves, hills, tunnels), scenery and traffic placed on it, `curveAt` throwing the car outward, a clock and checkpoints | ROAD |\n| Top-down racing and driving (Micro Machines, RC Pro-Am, GTA) | `topdown` / `iso` | `E.Car` on a TileMap (its floor tags slow it, its walls bounce it), `E.Race` for laps and drivers, cars drawn with `px.poly` on `r.w()` corner points | KART |\n| First-person shooter (Doom, GoldenEye 007, Apex Legends) | the 3D engine's first person (or third) | a level of text rows or a terrain, `world.ray` hitscan, recoil and reloads, doors (`world.thing('door')`), raiders on `world.flow()` | 3D SHOOTER |\n| Bomberman, Frogger, Sokoban, Gauntlet, Robotron; Sonic, Prince of Persia; light guns | as the recipe says | `AI_GUIDE.md`'s Genre recipes: each on the kit closest to it | (a recipe) |\n\n**Sizes:** heroes 40-60 px tall at 320x240 (`size: 1.2-1.4`), bosses 1.8-2.4. Small things (coins, bullets, ships, pickups) are string sprites designed at 8-16 px, drawn at scale 2 if they are the player's ship. Keep hitboxes smaller than the art.\n\n**Feel numbers** (world units per second, tile = 16): walk 70-90, run 95-140, jump 250-320 with gravity 800, fall cap 330, dash 200-260, bullets 250-320 (player) and 70-120 (enemy), enemy walk 25-45. Hit feedback: `game.hitFx` (Effects).\n\n## More: animation and examples outside this card\nThe repo (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge; any file at `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/<path>`) holds more to take from. Its files are large: search them and take only what the game needs. Real 3D (`E.World3D`: first person, racing, flight) is there: `engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js`.\n- **Motion clips**: 325 curated and 2,548 motion-capture takes that play on any Humanoid: find one in `src/mocap/catalogs/`, cut a small set with `tools/anim-set.mjs`, then `Mocap.drive(rig, lib)` (`AI_GUIDE.md`, Where to find more; `docs/MOCAP.md`).\n- **Objects and materials** (full engine): `r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing })` draws a still object from any view and facing, `map.solid(...)` makes it solid; `E.MATERIALS` dresses floors (`floorMat`), walls (`face`, `roof`) and platform tiles (`mat`). `docs/ASSETS.md` is the card: the format, the library, writing one and checking it with `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs`.\n- **Worked examples**: Emberdeep (`src/emberdeep/`), a whole game on this engine: 29 monster, boss and dummy bodies, 3 heroes and 30 skills, registered with `def(kind, id, spec)` (one search lists them); adapt them, they lean on the game's own helpers. `docs/CHARACTERS.md` is the recipe for a new body.\n- **Modules** (`engine/modules/<name>.js`; `modules/` in the handoff package): general systems in files of their own, each a `<script>` after the engine, its header its manual (read it there, or its section of the index). A kit carries the modules its slice names (`@modules` in its header); the full engine (`dist/my-3d2dge.js`; `my-3d2dge.js` in the handoff package) carries them all.\n  - `grid`: square and hex grids: A* paths, move ranges over heights and past allies, fields of view, `E.Fog`, groups, shapes of effect, threat maps, `E.GridMover`, `E.Turns` (speed, charge time, phases, ATB). ROGUELIKE, PUZZLE, TACTICS, ARCADE, ARTILLERY, RTS, SIM, 3D CRAWLER.\n  - `gen`: generated maps from a seed: rooms and corridors, BSP, caves, mazes, Poisson scatter, as ASCII rows a TileMap reads. ROGUELIKE, ARCADE.\n  - `fight` (the full engine only): one-on-one fighting: `E.Fighter` (frame data, hurt boxes from the rig's joints, guards, throws, cancels, juggles, specials by motion or charge, a meter, projectiles), `E.Match` (rounds, KO, the HUD, training), `E.FightAI`, `E.FightSelect`. FIGHTING.\n  - `rooms`: a world of rooms on a grid of screens (`E.World`): walking between them at open edges, the explored map (`drawMap`, or `shellMap()` for `E.Shell`), gates that abilities or keys open, saves in `E.store`. METROIDVANIA.\n  - `mode7`: the SNES's Mode 7 (`E.Mode7`): a camera over a flat floor (a TileMap's, a function's or a canvas), a turning sky, billboards far to near (rigs, sprites, shapes, your drawing), fog, `project` and `toFloor`, split screens. KART.\n  - `road`: the pseudo-3D road (`E.Road`): segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, tunnels, scenery and cars scaled by distance and hidden past a crest, the sky's parallax on curves. ROAD.\n  - `drive`: cars on the ground plane (`E.Car`: grip and slide, a kart's hop and drift boost, floor tags, walls and cars it bounces off) and races (`E.Race`: checkpoints along an `E.Path`, laps, places, drivers that pass and rubber-band, items, the HUD; the 3D engine's `world.vehicle` too). KART.\n  - `story`: dialogue as data (`E.Story`): lines with speakers and portraits, choices with conditions, flags and values, gotos, the game's events, a quest log, balloons over heads, a backlog, auto and skip; its state for a save. RPG, POINT-AND-CLICK, TACTICS.\n  - `rpg`: a role-playing game's rules (`E.RPG`): items, bags (slots or a grid of sizes), members with stats, levels and gear, status effects, a party (items used, rewards shared), shops, damage, random encounters by zone, list and card windows. RPG, 3D HORROR.\n  - `strategy` (the full engine only; needs `grid`): `E.Strategy` for real-time strategy (selection by click, box and group; queued orders; formations; production, resources, placement; fog, the minimap; an AI's build order and waves) and for sims `E.Clock` (days, the light), `E.needs` and `E.choose`, `E.overlay`, `E.tooltip`. RTS, SIM.\n  - `click` (the full engine only): point-and-click adventures (`E.Click`): painted rooms, walk areas with holes (`E.Walkbox`), depth scale, hotspots with verbs, SCUMM's nine verbs, Sierra's icons, a verb coin or two buttons, an inventory, rules as data, exits, `story`'s talk; taps on a phone. POINT-AND-CLICK.\n  - `physics`: 2D rigid bodies (`E.Physics`): circles, boxes, polygons, segments, chains and arcs; bounce, friction, sensors, layers, sleep; fast balls swept, never passing through; the same world at any refresh rate; flippers, bumpers, slingshots, kickers. PINBALL, ARTILLERY.\n  - `terrain`: destructible ground in the side plane (`E.Terrain`): carved and added by circles and polygons, the ground below a point and its normal, rays for shots, walkers on slopes, a collider for `physics`. ARTILLERY.\n  - `songs`: the songbook (`E.Songbook`): songs by mood (field, town, battle, race, horror, chase, dance ...) and jingles (stage clear, game over, level up); `get(id)`, `find(mood)`. RHYTHM.\n  - `rhythm` (the full engine only): `E.Rhythm`: charts on a song's steps, judgments in ms of the music clock, combo, score, a life gauge, grades, holds, call and response, a note highway in any direction. RHYTHM.\n  - `arcade`: the coin-op's frame: scores that float up, extra lives, two players taking turns, credits and a continue, high-score tables with initials on a letter wheel, stage cards, the attract mode (a demo, the table, the title). ARCADE, SHOOTER, PINBALL.\n- **Everything running**: https://my-3d2dge.vercel.app/labs\n\n## Before you hand the game back\n- One IIFE starting with `const E = My3D2dge` (between the markers in a single file; `game/game.js` in the handoff package). Only your game: no leftover starter menu or unused slices. No network, no libraries.\n- Title screen and game-over screen as scenes; `pausable: true` on gameplay scenes. No pause, settings, rebinding or full-screen code of your own (they're standard); prompts from `game.input.label(action)`.\n- The camera follows the player (`game.focus` every update) and shows the level; the HUD uses screen pixels, or `E.Shell`'s HTML for a modern game (the STEALTH kit; the handoff package's template).\n- Sound effects on jump, hit, pickup and death; music per scene.\n- The look target list above: backdrop, textured tiles, props, sized and dressed HD characters, effects, title font, lights. Compare your screenshots with Symphony of the Night or Metal Slug, not with NES games.\n- If you can run commands: `node tools/check.mjs game/index.html` (your page; add `#scene` to jump to a scene). It presses start, plays, cycles the views, prints how much of the screen is filled and how many colors it uses, adds look notes (flat areas, checkerboard dithering, low contrast, a thin palette), and fails on any error. Act on every look note. `node tools/filmstrip.mjs game/index.html#scene --steps \"wait:1500 press:Enter wait:800 rec:16:2 press:KeyJ\" --crop x,y,w,h` records an animation frame by frame into one contact sheet: check every attack with it (a swing must wind up, strike, and settle back without jerks or backward sweeps).\n- Animation variety: every character has its own moves from `E.MOVES` (not one shared swing), enemies telegraph with a visible wind-up, and reactions play out (hurt, knockback, `down`, victory `cheer`).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='src/content.js'\ns=open(p).read().replace(\\\"{wood:1,stone:2,reinforced:3.5}\\\",\\\"{wood:1.5,stone:4,reinforced:6}\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/sim.js';s=open(p).read();s=s.replace(\\\"const key=hit.target+hit.seat;if(record.disabled.includes(key)||p.protectUntil>w.time||disabled(w,p))return false;record.disabled.push(key);const prop=hit.target==='crew'?'crewUntil':'launcherUntil';\\\", \\\"const key=hit.target+hit.seat;const prop=hit.target==='crew'?'crewUntil':'launcherUntil';if(record.disabled.includes(key)||p.protectUntil>w.time||p[prop]+(p[prop]>0?w.config.protection:0)>w.time)return false;record.disabled.push(key);\\\")\n# Ignore withdrawn targets in physical collision. Other target can still be interrupted, endpoints combine by max.\ns=s.replace(\\\"const p=w.players[enemy];test(segmentCircle(s.x,s.z,X,Z,p.crewX,55,10+radius),1,'crew',{seat:enemy});test(segmentCircle(s.x,s.z,X,Z,p.x,55,15+radius),2,'launcher',{seat:enemy});\\\", \\\"const p=w.players[enemy];if(p.crewUntil<=w.time)test(segmentCircle(s.x,s.z,X,Z,p.crewX,55,10+radius),1,'crew',{seat:enemy});if(p.launcherUntil<=w.time)test(segmentCircle(s.x,s.z,X,Z,p.x,55,15+radius),2,'launcher',{seat:enemy});\\\")\n# author blocks contract\ns=s.replace(\\\"export function validateCourt(data){const errors=[];\\\", \\\"export function validateCourt(data){const errors=[];if(Array.isArray(data?.blocks)){if(data.version\"'!==1)errors.push('\"'Court version must be 1.');if(data.blocks.length<2||data.blocks.length>180)errors.push('Use 2–180 blocks.');const ids=new Set();for(const b of data.blocks){if(ids.has(b.id))errors.push('Block IDs must be unique.');ids.add(b.id);if(\"'![0,1].includes(b.seat)||![b.x,b.z,b.w,b.h,b.hp,b.maxHp].every(Number.isFinite)||b.w<4||b.h<4||b.x<30||b.x+b.w>610||b.z<30||b.z+b.h>205||!['\"'wood','stone','reinforced','foundation'].includes(b.material)||\"'!Array.isArray(b.supports))errors.push('\"'Invalid block dimensions, material or supports.');}for(const b of data.blocks)if(b.supports?.some(id=>\"'!ids.has(id)))errors.push('\"'Support ID is missing.');if(\"'!errors.length){const reached=connected({blocks:data.blocks});if(data.blocks.some(b=>b.alive&&!b.foundation&&!reached.has(b.id)))errors.push('\"'Every objective needs a foundation path.');for(const b of data.blocks.filter(b=>\"'!b.foundation)){const target=b.x+b.w/2,dx=Math.abs(target-(b.seat?150:490)),dz=b.z+b.h/2-70,den=2*Math.cos(angle)**2*(dx*Math.tan(angle)-dz);if(den<=0||Math.sqrt(120*dx*dx/den)>290)errors.push('\"'A block is outside the legal ballistic envelope.');}}return {valid:errors.length===0,errors};}\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncat > src/persistence.js <<'EOF'\nexport const NAMESPACE='smithereen-royal-rumble.v1';\nexport const SETTING_DEFAULTS={music:.10,effects:.7,voice:.45,mute:false,glyphs:'PlayStation',tension:1.4,prediction:false,reducedMotion:false,uiScale:1,fire1:'Space',fire2:'ShiftRight',seat1:'keyboard',seat2:'keyboard'};\nexport function readStorage(storage=globalThis.localStorage){try{return JSON.parse(storage.getItem(NAMESPACE)||'null');}catch{return null;}}\nexport function load(storage){const raw=readStorage(storage);const settings={...SETTING_DEFAULTS};if(raw?.version===1&&raw.settings&&typeof raw.settings==='object'){\n for(const key of ['music','effects','voice'])if(Number.isFinite(raw.settings[key]))settings[key]=Math.max(0,Math.min(1,raw.settings[key]));\n for(const key of ['mute','prediction','reducedMotion'])if(typeof raw.settings[key]==='boolean')settings[key]=raw.settings[key];\n if(['PlayStation','Xbox'].includes(raw.settings.glyphs))settings.glyphs=raw.settings.glyphs;\n if([1.4,1,.7].includes(raw.settings.tension))settings.tension=raw.settings.tension;\n if([.85,1,1.15,1.3].includes(raw.settings.uiScale))settings.uiScale=raw.settings.uiScale;\n for(const key of ['fire1','fire2'])if(typeof raw.settings[key]==='string'&&/\"'^(Space|ShiftRight|Key[A-Z]|Digit[0-9]|Enter|ControlRight)$/.test(raw.settings[key]))settings[key]=raw.settings[key];\n if(settings.fire1===settings.fire2)settings.fire2=settings.fire1==='\"'ShiftRight'?'Space':'ShiftRight';\n for(const key of ['seat1','seat2'])if(['keyboard','pad1','pad2','mouse'].includes(raw.settings[key]))settings[key]=raw.settings[key];\n }\n const t=raw?.tour;const tour=raw?.version===1&&t&&Number.isInteger(t.next)&&t.next>=1&&t.next<=10&&Number.isInteger(t.seed)&&Array.isArray(t.totals)&&t.totals.length===2&&t.totals.every(n=>Number.isFinite(n)&&n>=0)?{next:t.next,seed:t.seed,totals:t.totals,cheated:\"'!!t.cheated}:null;\n return {settings,tour};}\nexport function save(settings,tour,storage=globalThis.localStorage){try{storage.setItem(NAMESPACE,JSON.stringify({version:1,settings,tour}));return true;}catch{return false;}}\nEOF\ncat > metadata.json <<'\"'EOF'\n{\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-06 03:30:00\\\",\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Stone Sling Smithereens - 1980\\\",\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Action, Strategy, Sports; simultaneous artillery\\\",\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Fixed side-on 2D toy theatre\\\",\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"JavaScript ES modules; my-3D2dge 0.89.1 (8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691); AI Hub protocol 1 client 1.4.0 (35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869); esbuild 0.25.12 build only\\\",\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Original code-defined shaded pixel art in the engine native style: carved sectional castles, animated wooden catapults, heraldic crews, water and five medieval sporting courts; no external art\\\",\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Native E.Humanoid rigs and custom poses; state-driven catapult arm, rope, wheels, recoil, repair, retreat, protection, debris and surrender\\\",\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Code-only Web Audio music, impact and machinery effects, fanfares, and synthesized gibberish; separate buses; music defaults to 10%. Acoustic quality unknown without a listener\\\",\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"Two simultaneous local players on one screen; exactly two Hub players in one authoritative shared world, three-minute rounds. Online entry is provided by AI Hub; no standalone matchmaking\\\",\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Deterministic Node simulation and complete-tour drivers; native headless engine; Playwright 1.63.0 Chromium/WebKit/Firefox, controller stubs, touch profiles, two browser players and official Hub harness. No physical controller, touch device, iOS Safari, TV, remote human or listener available\\\",\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"Official Smithereens manual; native engine API, artillery kit and asset/animation guides; released Hub contract and official harness. Manual identifies 1982 and archive regional release 1981; supplied 1980 source label retained, discrepancy unresolved\\\",\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Codex CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort ultra\\\",\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\n  },\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\\"unknown\\\", \\\"unknown\\\", \\\"unknown\\\", \\\"unknown\\\"],\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\n    \\\"The dependency-free native renderer, shaded characters, props and exact fixed-step headless mode made a coherent self-contained game practical.\\\",\n    \\\"unknown\\\",\n    \\\"The authoritative simultaneous combat model, swept ballistics, support graph destruction, legal-command AI and Hub snapshot adapter.\\\",\n    \\\"Coordinating native shell input, independent local seats, responsive full-lane framing and a DOM-independent authoritative simulation.\\\",\n    \\\"No engine source changes; game-specific systems extend the full native engine and replace the artillery kit rules.\\\",\n    \\\"A documented multi-seat artillery adapter and a compact shared-world snapshot example would reduce integration work.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\n    \\\"The source identity, complete vertical-slice goal, delivery naming, reporting schema and hardware testing stand-ins were explicit.\\\",\n    \\\"The source year conflicts with historical references; the plan correctly requests keeping the supplied label without inventing a resolution.\\\",\n    \\\"Integrating complete tournament content, controller-first authoring tools and robust hosted authority into one offline artifact.\\\",\n    \\\"Separate mandatory acceptance cases from optional tuning targets, with a small machine-readable requirement checklist.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Smithereen Royal Rumble\\\",\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Hold your nerve. Lower their skyline.\\\",\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A simultaneous medieval artillery tournament across five destructible courts. Wind three kinds of stone, interrupt rival crews and topple supports through a ten-bout solo tour, same-screen local duels, or authoritative two-player Hub matches.\\\",\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Action\\\",\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Stone Sling Smithereens - 1980\\\",\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"\\\",\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–2\\\",\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Hold/release Space, mouse or Cross/A to fire; Q/E or L1/R1 stone; C/Circle cancels; Esc/Options pauses; local player 2 Right Shift and U/O; touch hold/release\\\",\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"2d\\\", \\\"arcade\\\", \\\"versus\\\", \\\"pixel art\\\", \\\"fantasy\\\", \\\"comedy\\\"]\n  }\n}\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
