{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"agent_message","text":"The scripted ten-bout run reached the championship, used every stone, caused both kinds of interruption and structural collapse, and verified the weighted totals. Phone review caught a framing bug that state tests missed: the engine’s minimum scale cropped the far castle. The view is being adjusted and checked in actual screen coordinates.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='src/main.js';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"game.settings.set('touch','off');game.input.touchEnabled=false;\\\", \\\"game.settings.set('touch','off');game.input.touchFilter=()=>false;game.input.touchEnabled=false;\\\");open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Integration and verification checkpoint\n- Native engine presentation, E.Shell TV UI, independent keyboard/pad/touch adapter, code-only three-bus audio, authoring/developer pages, and Hub authority are integrated. Deterministic build emits ~1.48 MB offline HTML and interview at required root paths.\n- Full tour driver reached all ten bouts and five courts, taught an actual hit, used all stones, both interruption targets, collapse, normal results and championship/replay. Included losses and weighted total reconciliation. First run: 123 assertions, one test-wait issue (launcher recovery still legitimately in progress); fixed the test wait. Production runtime bugs found during cross-module review fixed: fractional dev speed, settings persistence for bindings and pads, health-fraction tuning references, difficulty case mismatch, next-action charge duration lock, AI error slider scaling, and future target-return prediction.\n- Official Hub four cases passed: normal, latency150/jitter50/loss5, host-leave, server-without-player. Extra game-specific firing caught remote client paused by iframe blur during countdown; input agent corrected pre-start blur handling. Retest pending.\n- UI automated device checks initially 27/27 passed. Visual review found TV title last entries clipped and native START overlapping custom touch menu; fixed title composition and set native touch setting off for custom gesture ownership.\n- Phone visual review found cropped castles at native DPR1 minimum scale. View agent fixing with native custom side projection and adaptive320px portrait buffer; physical client-space bounds regression added.\n- Using touch:'never' to remove native START was an incorrect engine guess: it means unsupported touch and displays a blocking notice. Replaced with public settings touch=off plus custom gesture filter; no engine source changes.\n- Distinct observed browser bugs so far: clipped TV menu (medium), redundant native touch START (low), remote Hub pause before start (medium), cropped phone battlefield (high/game-breaking), touch-never unsupported overlay introduced during fix (high/game-breaking). Keep final bug count aligned with agent evidence.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='src/main.js';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"game.settings.set('touch','off');game.input.touchEnabled=false;\\\", \\\"game.settings.set('touch','off');game.input.touchFilter=()=>false;game.input.touchEnabled=false;\\\");open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Integration and verification checkpoint\n- Native engine presentation, E.Shell TV UI, independent keyboard/pad/touch adapter, code-only three-bus audio, authoring/developer pages, and Hub authority are integrated. Deterministic build emits ~1.48 MB offline HTML and interview at required root paths.\n- Full tour driver reached all ten bouts and five courts, taught an actual hit, used all stones, both interruption targets, collapse, normal results and championship/replay. Included losses and weighted total reconciliation. First run: 123 assertions, one test-wait issue (launcher recovery still legitimately in progress); fixed the test wait. Production runtime bugs found during cross-module review fixed: fractional dev speed, settings persistence for bindings and pads, health-fraction tuning references, difficulty case mismatch, next-action charge duration lock, AI error slider scaling, and future target-return prediction.\n- Official Hub four cases passed: normal, latency150/jitter50/loss5, host-leave, server-without-player. Extra game-specific firing caught remote client paused by iframe blur during countdown; input agent corrected pre-start blur handling. Retest pending.\n- UI automated device checks initially 27/27 passed. Visual review found TV title last entries clipped and native START overlapping custom touch menu; fixed title composition and set native touch setting off for custom gesture ownership.\n- Phone visual review found cropped castles at native DPR1 minimum scale. View agent fixing with native custom side projection and adaptive320px portrait buffer; physical client-space bounds regression added.\n- Using touch:'never' to remove native START was an incorrect engine guess: it means unsupported touch and displays a blocking notice. Replaced with public settings touch=off plus custom gesture filter; no engine source changes.\n- Distinct observed browser bugs so far: clipped TV menu (medium), redundant native touch START (low), remote Hub pause before start (medium), cropped phone battlefield (high/game-breaking), touch-never unsupported overlay introduced during fix (high/game-breaking). Keep final bug count aligned with agent evidence.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '100,120p' src/audio.js && cat tests/ui-input.py | head -n 55 && cat tests/hub-browser.py | tail -n 70 && sed -n '1,80p' src/view.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '100,120p' src/audio.js && cat tests/ui-input.py | head -n 55 && cat tests/hub-browser.py | tail -n 70 && sed -n '1,80p' src/view.js\"","aggregated_output":"    A.duck(['pause','settings','about','controls','developer','author'].includes(app.screen));\n  }\n  async function renderProbe(options={}) {\n    const OC=globalThis.OfflineAudioContext||globalThis.webkitOfflineAudioContext;if(!OC)return{supported:false,reason:'OfflineAudioContext unavailable'};\n    const ctx=new OC(2,48000*2,48000),master=ctx.createGain();master.gain.value=.7;master.connect(ctx.destination);\n    const buses={};for(const key of ['music','effects','voice']){buses[key]=ctx.createGain();buses[key].gain.value=options[key]??volumes[key];buses[key].connect(master);}\n    // Schedule the production native instrument and production effect patches on an offline synth copy.\n    const offline=Object.create(A);offline.ctx=ctx;offline._rnd=E.rng(37);offline._waves={};\n    offline._noise=ctx.createBuffer(1,ctx.sampleRate,ctx.sampleRate);const noiseData=offline._noise.getChannelData(0);for(let i=0;i<noiseData.length;i++)noiseData[i]=offline._rnd()*2-1;\n    MELODY.slice(0,8).forEach((n,i)=>{if(n)A._ins['rumble-lute'](ctx,buses.music,.02+i*.18,midi(n),.16,.2);});\n    for(const [id,t]of [['rumble-release',.1],['rumble-heavy',.55]])for(const patch of A.presets[id])offline._voice(patch,buses.effects,t,1,false);\n    babble(ctx,buses.voice,1.12,2,.09);\n    const buffer=await ctx.startRendering();let peak=0,sum=0,finite=true,count=0;\n    for(let ch=0;ch<buffer.numberOfChannels;ch++)for(const v of buffer.getChannelData(ch)){if(!Number.isFinite(v))finite=false;peak=Math.max(peak,Math.abs(v));sum+=v*v;count++;}\n    return{supported:true,finite,peak,rms:Math.sqrt(sum/count),nonzero:peak>0.00001,clipped:peak>=1,frames:buffer.length,gains:Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(buses).map(([k,b])=>[k,b.gain.value]))};\n  }\n  return {unlock,update,event,stop,setVolumes,renderProbe,diagnostics:()=>({unlocked,stopped,context:A.ctx?.state||'unavailable',musicGain:A.musicVolume,effectsGain:A.sfxVolume,voiceGain:A.voiceVolume,masterGain:A.volume,muted:A.muted,activeVoices:sources.size,counts:{...counts},files:0})};\n}\nimport json,pathlib,sys\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\nbase=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nchecks=0\nfailures=[]\ndef check(test,message):\n global checks\n checks+=1\n if not test: failures.append(message)\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n browser=p.chromium.launch(headless=True)\n page=browser.new_page(viewport={'width':1920,'height':1080})\n errors=[]\n page.on('pageerror',lambda e:errors.append(str(e)))\n page.goto((base/'index.html').as_uri())\n page.wait_for_function('window.__rumble && window.__rumble.ui')\n check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.screen')=='title','title boots')\n check(page.locator('.esh-ttl h1').inner_text()=='Smithereen Royal Rumble','native Shell title text')\n page.screenshot(path=str(base/'artifacts/ui-tv-title.png'))\n last_button=page.locator('.esh-btns>button').last.bounding_box()\n check(last_button['y']+last_button['height']<1045,'TV title keeps all actions inside safe area')\n page.keyboard.press('ArrowDown')\n check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.focus')==1,'one key moves focus exactly once')\n page.keyboard.press('Enter')\n page.wait_for_function('window.__rumble.screen === \"setup\"')\n check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.focus')==0,'setup starts with primary focus')\n page.keyboard.press('Enter')\n page.wait_for_function('window.__rumble.screen === \"play\"')\n page.wait_for_timeout(150)\n page.keyboard.down('Space');page.wait_for_timeout(600)\n power=page.evaluate('window.__rumble.world.players[0].charge?.power')\n check(power is not None and .2<power<.7,'human hold changes real charge')\n page.keyboard.up('Space');page.wait_for_timeout(150)\n check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.world.stats.shots[0]')==1,'human release launches exactly once')\n page.keyboard.press('Escape');page.wait_for_timeout(120)\n check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.screen')=='pause','Escape opens pause')\n t=page.evaluate('window.__rumble.world.time');page.wait_for_timeout(200)\n check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.world.time')==t,'standalone pause freezes sim')\n page.keyboard.press('Escape');page.wait_for_timeout(120)\n check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.screen')=='play','Escape closes pause')\n page.keyboard.down('Space');page.wait_for_timeout(80);page.keyboard.press('Escape');page.keyboard.up('Space');page.wait_for_timeout(80)\n shots=page.evaluate('window.__rumble.world.stats.shots[0]')\n page.keyboard.press('Escape');page.wait_for_timeout(1100)\n check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.world.stats.shots[0]')==shots,'pause cancels held input without a shot')\n page.evaluate('window.__rumble.start(\"local\", {court:0})');page.wait_for_timeout(200)\n page.keyboard.down('Space');page.keyboard.down('ShiftRight');page.wait_for_timeout(500)\n check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.world.players.every(p=>p.charge!==null)'),'independent local holds')\n page.keyboard.up('ShiftRight');page.wait_for_timeout(100)\n check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.world.players[0].charge!==null && window.__rumble.world.players[1].charge===null'),'right release preserves left charge')\n page.keyboard.up('Space');page.wait_for_timeout(100)\n check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.world.stats.shots.join(\",\")')=='1,1','both local releases launch once')\n page.evaluate('window.__rumble.pause();window.__rumble.ui.open(\"settings\");')\n page.wait_for_timeout(100)\n page.keyboard.press('ArrowDown');page.keyboard.press('ArrowRight');page.wait_for_timeout(50)\n check(abs(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.settings.music')-.15)<1e-8,'settings slider adjusts music')\n                for frame in frames\n            ]\n            check(\n                all(a[\"shots\"] == [1, 1] for a in actual),\n                \"Hub Fire: simultaneous holds/releases launch exactly once for each seat\",\n            )\n            check(\n                all(a[\"d\"][\"maxBytes\"] < 16384 for a in actual),\n                \"Hub Fire: actual gameplay messages stay bounded\",\n            )\n            page.wait_for_timeout(5000)\n            final_shapes = [\n                frame.evaluate(\n                    \"window.__rumble.world.blocks.map(b=>b.alive?1:0).join('')\"\n                )\n                for frame in frames\n            ]\n            check(\n                final_shapes[0] == final_shapes[1],\n                \"Hub Fire: gameplay destruction agrees under latency/jitter/loss\",\n            )\n            page.locator(\"#timeup\").click()\n            page.wait_for_function(\n                \"\"\"() => [...document.querySelectorAll('#grid iframe')].every(f => f.contentWindow.__rumble?.hubEnded)\"\"\",\n                timeout=8000,\n            )\n            before = [\n                frame.evaluate(\"window.__rumble.online.diagnostics().sent\")\n                for frame in frames\n            ]\n            for frame in frames:\n                frame.evaluate(\n                    \"window.__rumble.command(window.__rumble.hubSeat, {type:'begin'})\"\n                )\n            page.wait_for_timeout(300)\n            after = [\n                frame.evaluate(\"window.__rumble.online.diagnostics().sent\")\n                for frame in frames\n            ]\n            check(\n                before == after,\n                \"Hub Fire: no messages after end despite attempted input\",\n            )\n            evidence.append(\n                {\n                    \"case\": \"game-specific-simultaneous-fire\",\n                    \"copies\": actual,\n                    \"initialStates\": initial_states,\n                    \"begins\": begins,\n                    \"finalShapesAgree\": final_shapes[0] == final_shapes[1],\n                }\n            )\n        finally:\n            browser.close()\nexcept Exception as error:  # noqa: BLE001 - suite records the failure before shutting down its own server\n    check(False, f\"Hub browser suite: {type(error).__name__}: {error}\")\nfinally:\n    server.shutdown()\n    server.server_close()\n    thread.join(timeout=2)\n    (ARTIFACTS / \"hub-browser.json\").write_text(\n        json.dumps(\n            {\"checks\": checks, \"failures\": failures, \"evidence\": evidence}, indent=2\n        )\n    )\n\nfor failure in failures:\n    print(failure, file=sys.stderr)\nprint(f\"{checks} checks, {len(failures)} failures\")\nsys.exit(1 if failures else 0)\nimport { predict, health } from './sim.js';\n\nconst COURT_LOOKS = [\n  { name: 'VILLAGE EXHIBITION', sky: ['#325984','#8fbed0','#f3dbc1'], hills: '#789d8a', far: '#a2b6a2', earth: '#654c3d', stone: '#c5ae89', sun: '#ffe7a3', mood: 'day' },\n  { name: 'THE QUARRY MEET', sky: ['#697c96','#c3c6b3','#f4dec1'], hills: '#a79a87', far: '#c7bba0', earth: '#79604b', stone: '#ddd0a6', sun: '#fff1bf', mood: 'quarry' },\n  { name: 'THE HIGH KEEP', sky: ['#424b78','#ae9ab0','#eed1ad'], hills: '#686f83', far: '#9696a1', earth: '#4b4656', stone: '#aaa5b6', sun: '#f8d5a0', mood: 'keep' },\n  { name: 'LAKESIDE NIGHT COURT', sky: ['#121a3a','#28385c','#706479'], hills: '#303c54', far: '#444f6a', earth: '#333044', stone: '#aaa3a5', sun: '#e2e6c8', mood: 'night' },\n  { name: 'THE ROYAL FINAL', sky: ['#3e3e71','#af7895','#edb88c'], hills: '#686279', far: '#9b8c9b', earth: '#4c3b4b', stone: '#dac4a0', sun: '#ffdfa0', mood: 'royal' },\n];\nconst TEAMS = [\n  { color: '#55c7df', dark: '#245477', bright: '#c7f4ec', name: 'THE AZURE STAGS', sign: 'I' },\n  { color: '#f48466', dark: '#823c48', bright: '#ffe0a1', name: 'THE SCARLET BOARS', sign: 'II' },\n];\nconst STONE_NAMES = ['ROUNDSTONE','MASONRY','SPLIT STONE'];\nconst STONE_COLORS = ['#e2d6ba','#b2b9c4','#e6be58'];\nconst clamp = (n,a,b) => Math.max(a,Math.min(b,n));\nconst hash = n => { n = Math.imul(n ^ (n >>> 16),0x45d9f3b); n = Math.imul(n ^ (n >>> 16),0x45d9f3b); return ((n ^ (n >>> 16)) >>> 0)/4294967296; };\n\nexport function createView(E,game) {\n  const {px} = E;\n  const rigs = [], helpers = [], crowds = [];\n  let lastWorld = null, lastEvent = 0, clock = 0, fitKey = '', cachedPrediction = null, predictionKey = '';\n  let debris = [], splashes = [], rings = [], trails = new Map(), blockState = new Map(), releases = [0,0], wounds = [0,0], repairNoise = [0,0];\n  let lastR = null, touchLayouts = [], compactMode = null;\n  const compactView = new E.View('rumble-side','Tournament side',0,0,.9,1);\n  const materialCache = new Set();\n  E.Humanoid.pose('rumble-haul',(J,w,rig) => {\n    const k = Math.sin(rig.phase*2 + clock*12), target = {handL:[8,-3,13+k*1.4],handR:[9,3,14-k*1.4],elbowL:[3,-4,15],elbowR:[4,4,17]};\n    for (const id in target) if(J[id]) for(let a=0;a<3;a++) J[id][a] += (target[id][a]-J[id][a])*w;\n  });\n  E.Humanoid.pose('rumble-tool',(J,w) => {\n    for(const [id,target] of Object.entries({handL:[6,-3,12],handR:[9,3,18+Math.sin(clock*15)*5],elbowR:[5,4,19]})) if(J[id]) for(let a=0;a<3;a++) J[id][a]+=(target[a]-J[id][a])*w;\n  });\n  E.Humanoid.pose('rumble-flag',(J,w) => {\n    for(const [id,target] of Object.entries({handL:[5,-3,15],handR:[6,3,24],elbowR:[3,4,18]})) if(J[id]) for(let a=0;a<3;a++) J[id][a]+=(target[a]-J[id][a])*w;\n  });\n  E.SHAPES['rumble-block'] = { about:'A destructible tournament wall section',mats:{s:'sandstone'},params:{w:18,h:18},make:p=>[['box','s',[0,0,0],[p.w,6,p.h]]] };\n  E.SHAPES['rumble-buttress'] = { about:'Court boundary marker',mats:{s:'slate',g:'gold'},parts:[['box','s',[0,0,0],[8,7,12]],['box','g',[0,0,12],[10,9,2]]] };\n  for(let seat=0;seat<2;seat++) {\n    const T=TEAMS[seat];\n    rigs.push(new E.Humanoid({size:.92,weapon:null,outfit:'tunic',hair:seat?'short':'ponytail',hat:{style:'helmet',color:'#c2bba5'},armor:true,cape:{len:5,width:4},sleeves:'long',colors:{skin:seat?'#cc956d':'#e5ba91',hair:seat?'#593c37':'#4d3333',cloth:T.color,coat:T.dark,pants:'#443b48',boot:'#322e38',belt:'#b08a51',trim:T.bright,glove:'#c7a474',cape:T.color,capeIn:T.dark,metal:'#b4bac0',plate:'#9399a1'}}));\n    helpers.push(new E.Humanoid({size:.73,weapon:null,outfit:'shirt',hair:'short',hat:{style:'cap',color:T.color},sleeves:'short',colors:{skin:'#d7a17c',cloth:T.dark,pants:'#6d5b54',boot:'#40383d',trim:T.bright,hair:'#4b3530'}}));\n  }\n  for(let i=0;i<14;i++) crowds.push(new E.Humanoid({size:.44,style:'hd',weapon:null,outfit:i%3?'tunic':'robe',hair:'short',hat:i%4===0?'pointed':i%4===1?'cap':null,colors:{skin:['#dbb48c','#b97b60','#e0ba9c'][i%3],cloth:['#c68b5b','#6e9a8b','#b06c78','#7674a1','#c3aa69'][i%5],pants:'#554a4e',boot:'#3c3541',hair:'#614b3e'}}));\n  game.cam.smooth=0;\n  game.lights.enabled=true;\n  game.particles.ground=(x,y,z)=>x<245||x>395?40:19;\n  function fit() {\n    const rect=game.screen.canvas?.getBoundingClientRect(),compact=!!rect&&(rect.width<620||rect.height>rect.width*1.2);\n    if(compact!==compactMode){compactMode=compact;game.screen.setOptions({res:compact?[320,180]:[640,360]});game.setView(compact?compactView:E.VIEWS.side);fitKey='';}\n    const W=game.W,H=game.H,key=`${W}:${H}`;\n    if(key!==fitKey) {\n      fitKey=key;\n      game.setZoom(clamp((W-30)/(640*(compact?.9:1.5)),.5,1.4));\n      game.cam.bounds=null;game.cam.offset=[0,0];game.cam.snap=true;\n    }\n    game.focus(320,0,175);\n  }\n  function clear() {\n    lastWorld=null;lastEvent=0;debris=[];splashes=[];rings=[];trails.clear();blockState.clear();releases=[0,0];wounds=[0,0];cachedPrediction=null;predictionKey='';game.particles.clear?.();\n  }\n  function process(e,app) {\n    const x=Number.isFinite(e.x)?e.x:(app.world.players[e.seat||0]?.x||320),z=Number.isFinite(e.z)?e.z:55;\n    if(e.type==='launch') {releases[e.seat||0]=.38; game.particles.dust(x,0,40,4);}\n    if(e.type==='impact'||e.type==='hit') {\n      const water=e.target==='water';\n      rings.push({x,z,t:0,life:.48,color:water?'#a4e3ec':'#ffe6aa',size:water?18:12});\n      if(water) splashes.push({x,z,t:0});\n      else { game.particles.bits(x,0,z,app.settings.reducedMotion?3:9,['#c9b08c','#edd5a2','#827568']);game.particles.dust(x,0,z,app.settings.reducedMotion?2:7); }\n      if(!app.settings.reducedMotion && e.target!=='water') game.shake(e.stone===1||e.projectileType===1?2.3:1.1);\n    }\n    if(e.type==='crew'||e.type==='launcher'||e.type==='interrupt') {wounds[e.targetSeat??e.seat??0]=.5;game.particles.impact(x,0,z,9,'#ffe8a1');}\n    if(e.type==='recover') {game.particles.glints(x,0,z,8,'#abf4e1');rings.push({x,z,t:0,life:.8,color:'#a9f7dc',size:25});}\n    if(e.type==='split') {game.particles.glints(x,0,z,7,'#ffe29b');rings.push({x,z,t:0,life:.5,color:'#ffda78',size:14});}\n    if(e.type==='outcome') {for(let i=0;i<2;i++) game.particles.glints(app.world.players[i].x,0,90,9,TEAMS[i].bright);}\n  }\n  function update(dt,app) {\n    clock+=dt;fit();\n    const w=app.world;if(!w)return;\n    touchLayouts=[];app.touchChips=[];\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > tests/browser.py <<'EOF'\nimport json\nimport pathlib\nimport sys\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\n\nbase = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nproject = json.loads((base / 'project.json').read_text())\nartifact = base.parent / (project['basename'] + '.html')\nchecks, failures = 0, []\nevidence = {}\n\n\ndef check(value, message):\n    global checks\n    checks += 1\n    if not value:\n        failures.append(message)\n\n\ntry:\n    with sync_playwright() as p:\n        browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=True)\n        context = browser.new_context(viewport={'width': 1920, 'height': 1080})\n        page = context.new_page()\n        errors, requests = [], []\n        page.on('pageerror', lambda error: errors.append(str(error)))\n        page.on('request', lambda request: requests.append(request.url))\n        page.goto(artifact.as_uri())\n        page.wait_for_function('window.__rumble && window.__rumble.ui')\n        check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.screen') == 'title', 'exact final file boots at title')\n        check(page.title() == project['title'], 'published title matches metadata')\n        check(not errors, 'fresh final artifact has no page errors')\n        check(all(url.startswith('file:') or url.startswith('data:') for url in requests), 'standalone makes no network requests')\n        check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.settings.music') == .1, 'fresh music defaults to ten percent')\n        page.keyboard.press('Enter')\n        page.wait_for_function('window.__rumble.screen === \\\"play\\\"')\n        check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.world.bout === 1 && window.__rumble.mode === \\\"solo\\\"'), 'title primary action enters actual solo bout')\n        page.keyboard.down('Space')\n        page.wait_for_function('window.__rumble.world.players[0].charge?.power >= .5')\n        page.screenshot(path=str(base / 'artifacts/final-charged-combat.png'))\n        page.keyboard.up('Space')\n        page.wait_for_function('window.__rumble.world.stats.shots[0] === 1')\n        check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.world.stats.shots[0]') == 1, 'final artifact human hold-release launches once')\n        page.evaluate('window.__rumble.game.advance(7)')\n        check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.world.events.some(e=>e.type===\\\"impact\\\")'), 'final artifact shot resolves against real targets')\n        probes = page.evaluate('''async () => {\n            const a = window.__rumble.audio;\n            return {mix:await a.renderProbe(),silent:await a.renderProbe({music:0,effects:0,voice:0}),music:await a.renderProbe({music:.1,effects:0,voice:0}),effects:await a.renderProbe({music:0,effects:.7,voice:0}),voice:await a.renderProbe({music:0,effects:0,voice:.45}),diagnostics:a.diagnostics()};\n        }''')\n        evidence['audio'] = probes\n        for bus in ['mix', 'music', 'effects', 'voice']:\n            check(probes[bus].get('finite') and probes[bus].get('nonzero'), f'production {bus} offline audio is finite and nonzero')\n            check(not probes[bus].get('clipped'), f'production {bus} representative audio does not clip')\n        check(probes['silent'].get('peak') == 0, 'muted independent audio buses yield silence')\n        check(probes['music']['gains']['music'] == .1, 'offline music routes through exactly ten percent gain')\n        # Complete a real duel through legal AI, then inspect actual result and replay.\n        page.evaluate('''() => {const a=window.__rumble;a.start('quick',{court:4,difficulty:'hard',seed:91});a.world.players[0].ai={style:'mason',reaction:.3,error:0,perfect:true,breadth:81,next:.4};a.game.advance(92);}''')\n        check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.world.phase') == 'over', 'final artifact real combat reaches a natural outcome')\n        check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.screen') == 'result', 'natural outcome opens result menu')\n        check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.world.stats.shots.every(n=>n>0)'), 'both duel players fire through legal simulation')\n        check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.world.stats.collapses') > 0, 'final artifact duel demonstrates structural collapse')\n        page.screenshot(path=str(base / 'artifacts/final-result.png'))\n        page.keyboard.press('Enter')\n        page.wait_for_function('window.__rumble.screen === \\\"play\\\" && window.__rumble.world.phase === \\\"play\\\"')\n        check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.world.stats.shots.join(\\\",\\\")') == '0,0', 'result rematch clears old projectiles and scores')\n        page.evaluate('window.__rumble.pause();window.__rumble.ui.open(\\\"about\\\");')\n        check(page.locator('.esh-sh').inner_text().find('Source Information') >= 0, 'credits source information is reachable')\n        page.screenshot(path=str(base / 'artifacts/final-credits.png'))\n        check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.game.errors.length') == 0, 'native browser engine reports no errors')\n        check(not errors, 'complete final artifact path has no page errors')\n        evidence['chromium'] = {'errors': errors, 'requests': requests, 'snapshot': page.evaluate('window.__rumble.snapshot()')}\n        context.close()\n        browser.close()\n        # Closest available approximation to a touch-only iPhone, native Canvas path.\n        browser = p.webkit.launch(headless=True)\n        context = browser.new_context(**p.devices['iPhone 13'])\n        page = context.new_page()\n        errors = []\n        page.on('pageerror', lambda error: errors.append(str(error)))\n        page.goto(artifact.as_uri())\n        page.wait_for_function('window.__rumble && window.__rumble.ui')\n        check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.screen') == 'title', 'WebKit phone final artifact boots')\n        page.get_by_role('button', name='Solo Tour', exact=False).click()\n        page.wait_for_function('window.__rumble.screen === \\\"play\\\"')\n        check(page.locator('[data-sys=\\\"need\\\"]').count() == 0, 'touch-only play has no unsupported-device blocker')\n        check(page.locator('[data-act=\\\"menu\\\"]').count() == 0, 'custom touch menu has no inherited START overlay')\n        # Hardware portrait bounds, rather than just internal buffer coordinates.\n        bounds = page.evaluate('''() => { const a=window.__rumble,g=a.game,s=g.screen,c=s.canvas,r=c.getBoundingClientRect(),v=g.view;return [40,600].map(x=>{const p=v.p(x,0,40);return r.left+((p[0]-s.ix)*s.S+s.OX)/c.width*r.width}); }''')\n        check(all(0 <= x <= 390 for x in bounds), 'WebKit phone fits both castle foundations in physical screen')\n        page.dispatch_event('#screen', 'pointerdown', {'pointerId': 31, 'pointerType': 'touch', 'clientX': 90, 'clientY': 600, 'button': 0, 'buttons': 1})\n        page.wait_for_function('window.__rumble.world.players[0].charge?.power > .25')\n        page.dispatch_event('#screen', 'pointerup', {'pointerId': 31, 'pointerType': 'touch', 'clientX': 90, 'clientY': 600, 'button': 0, 'buttons': 0})\n        page.wait_for_function('window.__rumble.world.stats.shots[0] === 1')\n        check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.device') == 'touch', 'WebKit touch hold-release chooses touch prompts')\n        page.dispatch_event('#screen', 'pointerdown', {'pointerId': 32, 'pointerType': 'touch', 'clientX': 90, 'clientY': 600, 'button': 0, 'buttons': 1})\n        page.wait_for_timeout(100)\n        page.dispatch_event('#screen', 'pointercancel', {'pointerId': 32, 'pointerType': 'touch', 'clientX': 90, 'clientY': 600, 'button': 0, 'buttons': 0})\n        page.wait_for_timeout(150)\n        check(page.evaluate('window.__rumble.world.stats.shots[0]') == 1, 'pointer cancellation never emits extra shot')\n        check(not errors and page.evaluate('window.__rumble.game.errors.length') == 0, 'WebKit phone native canvas/input without errors')\n        evidence['webkitPhone'] = {'bounds': bounds, 'errors': errors}\n        context.close()\n        browser.close()\n        browser = p.firefox.launch(headless=True)\n        page = browser.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720})\n        errors = []\n        page.on('pageerror', lambda error: errors.append(str(error)))\n        page.goto(artifact.as_uri())\n        page.wait_for_function('window.__rumble && window.__rumble.ui')\n        page.keyboard.press('Enter')\n        page.wait_for_function('window.__rumble.screen === \\\"play\\\"')\n        page.evaluate('window.__rumble.game.advance(1)')\n        check(not errors and page.evaluate('window.__rumble.game.errors.length') == 0, 'Firefox Canvas gameplay needs no WebGL')\n        evidence['firefox'] = {'errors': errors}\n        browser.close()\nexcept Exception as error:\n    check(False, f'Browser/artifact suite: {type(error).__name__}: {error}')\n\n(base / 'artifacts/browser.json').write_text(json.dumps({'checks': checks, 'failures': failures, 'evidence': evidence}, indent=2))\nfor failure in failures:\n    print(failure, file=sys.stderr)\nprint(f'{checks} checks, {len(failures)} failures')\nsys.exit(1 if failures else 0)\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
