{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"head -n 45 tests/view-browser.mjs && tail -n 20 tests/view-browser.mjs && cat > REQUIREMENTS.md <<'EOF'\n# Requirement and evidence ledger\n\nThe complete specification is in ../PLAN.md and ../TASK.md. These rows group related requirements without dropping their distinct acceptance paths.\n\n| Area | Implementation | Observed acceptance |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Native engine / packaging | Full 0.89.1 handoff, adapted artillery fixed-step/predictor design, native View/px/materials/props/Humanoid/Shell/ChipAudio; scripts/build.mjs | tests/artifact.mjs: exact released Hub bytes first, three inline scripts, no runtime asset URLs/absolute paths, metadata schema; exact final file tested |\n| Simultaneous charge | sim.js command state machine, capped power, fixed50° elevation, charge-time presets, stone lock, cancel/buffer/reload | simulation.mjs short/full holds, independent simultaneous releases, no unwanted buffer shots; ui-input.py human key/pad/touch cancellation |\n| Ballistics | Analytic per-step integration plus segment sweep; same production predictor; split at apex; explicit z-up boundary | Prediction/live agreement all stones both seats, thin-block sweep, all courts' exposed last fragments reachable, no NaN |\n| Objective destruction | Stable material blocks, authored directed support paths/foundations, atomic tick impacts and removal, visual debris | Real cascade without score farming, foundations persist, all5 AI courts finish, full tour collapses, browser actual duel demolition |\n| Tactical interruption | Crew retreat1.8s, launcher repair2.6s, endpoint max, input cancel, protected return1.25s, throw dedup | Both targets through real shots; overlap/protection/no queued shot fixtures; actual full tour both target kinds |\n| Scoring/outcomes | 3/7/13 direct score, winner × bout, loser0, mutual draw,90s normalized-health then score, frozen next actions | Unit ties/outcomes/exactly-once and full10 weighted total reconciliation; browser natural result/rematch |\n| Three stones | Round precision, masonry2.6 damage, deterministic3-way split, remembered range per type | All stone predictor/live runs and complete tour coverage, touch/keyboard/pad switching; native distinct art/audio |\n| Content / tour | Five different support layouts/moods, ten authored personalities, advance after loss, championship | Actual legal-command tour enters each court/bout, lesson shot+hit, losses advance, save clears at finish, replay begins1 |\n| AI | Common legal command interface; production trajectory search, support value, tactical protection at arrival; profile reaction/error | Deterministic all5-court completion; ordinary AI never writes hp/score; bounded search refinements for remnants |\n| Devices / TV | Native Shell menus, focus ring/hover, controller polling and explicit local seat assignments, last-device prompts, rebindable keys | ui-input.py two independent keys, two pads, disconnect pause, UI navigation, sliders; title/phone captures reviewed |\n| Touch / narrow display | Custom captured pointer holds, cancellation, contextual stone chips/halo; compact native side projection keeps whole lane | Physical client-space bounds regression, real CDP hold/release and chip tap, WebKit iPhone profile and pointercancel |\n| Settings / safety | Game-specific validated storage, three sound buses/mute, glyphs/tension/prediction/assist/reduced motion/UI scale, safe focus cancel | Corrupt/old/denied storage; settings retained; native START and unsupported-touch blocker regressions; gameplay never depends on audio |\n| Attract | Exact10s front-menu idle threshold, throwaway real bot world, all stones/courts, consumed exit | Exact before/at threshold assertions, shot state observed, no tour writes, keyboard/pad/touch exit coverage |\n| Developer | Pause workshop, scenario/AI seats/court/bout, restore/clear/result, pause/step/speed/invulnerability, collision/support/arc | UI navigation and tuning checks, fractional speed and exact step tests, cheated runs marked; hosted diagnostics read-only |\n| Court authoring | Version1 editable blocks, material/foundation/support fields, validation/import/export/apply/preview | Valid default roundtrip, malformed support/dimensions rejected, ballistic envelope and connectivity checked; UI author apply/export/import |\n| Code-only audio | Native synth custom instrument/patches plus formant gibberish, three buses, music.10 | Production offline music/effects/voice/mix nonzero finite, representative peak<1, all-bus mute0; acoustic quality unconfirmed |\n| Hub lifecycle | Active boot bypass, automatic ready, negative-clock wait, authoritative host incl no local seat, reliable intents/snapshots/ACKs, deadline/leave/end | Official harness normal/adverse150±50ms5%loss/host-leave/server cases; __hubCheck.pass and body complete; extra simultaneous firing match |\n| Hub fairness/traffic | Authenticated from->seat, seq/duration validation, bounded FIFO retry/cancel reserve, compact hp state, final ACK barrier | hub-unit.mjs duplicate/forgery/rejected-send/reorder tests; max snapshot and packet budget; both confirmed shots and silhouettes agree; no input/audio/messages after end |\n| Reports | metadata.json is sole source for game and root exit-interview.json | JSON parse/key/type/order checks, exact model/date/environment/usage, catalogue title/control/player consistency |\n\n## Refinements and justified implementation choices\n\n- Kept engine source unchanged. Custom game systems replace inherited walking, turn queue, angle adjustment, wind, rockets and inventory, following the plan.\n- Increased material health after initial native AI play ended in15–25s. The initial complete-tour driver then ran about14min of simulated bout time; subsequent tactical AI refinement favors castle targets for mason/broad personalities. A skilled bot is not a first-time human timing measurement.\n- Native Shell is retained, with custom simultaneous-seat routing so one confirm/fire cannot control both seats. Its touch controls are set off through native settings because the game supplies contact holds and a contextual stone selector.\n- Compact phone composition uses a public native custom View and320px buffer to avoid fixed-resolution minimum-scale cropping. Physics and collision are identical.\n- Local courts author editable block graphs rather than requiring full rigid-body settling. Unsupported blocks immediately leave objective/collision state and become finite cosmetic debris, as specified.\n- Hub uses periodic full compact dynamic state rather than fragile lossy block deltas. Static geometry regenerates from court/config; every passive client acknowledges reliable baselines. The host waits for final-state ACKs within supplied grace.\n- Standalone has same-device versus. Internet play is entered through AI Hub; no nonfunctional room browser is presented.\n- Validation uses documented stand-ins: no physical controller, touch hardware, TV, remote player, listener, or real iOS Safari was available.\nEOF\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Smithereen Royal Rumble\n\nOpen the HTML in the parent folder directly. It is self-contained and works offline. Hosted online play is entered by AI Hub; standalone supports solo and simultaneous same-device versus.\n\nHold **Space / left mouse / Cross** to wind. Release to throw. Watch the landing marker: full tension overshoots. **Q/E / L1/R1** changes stone; **C / right mouse / Circle** cancels. **Escape / Options** opens pause. Keyboard player two uses **Right Shift** and **U/O**. Touch holds in the friendly half and releases to throw; contextual arrows select stones. Controls can be rebound, glyphs changed to Xbox, and timing assistance enabled in Settings.\n\nA castle is the objective. Crew and launcher hits interrupt briefly, then return with visible protection. Unsupported sections collapse. A ten-bout tour advances after defeat and banks the winning direct score times the bout number. The last bouts carry more weight.\n\n\"'`npm ci` installs pinned build/test dependencies (no browser download needed on this workstation). `npm run build` deterministically publishes the exact single HTML and exit-interview.json to the parent folder, using metadata.json as the source for both credits and interview. `npm run verify` runs simulation, complete-tour, devices, artifact, production audio and official Hub harness checks, printing only failures and one count. Python Playwright uses the installed workstation venv; Node Playwright is pinned1.63.0 and uses the already installed browsers.\n\nDeveloper tools are available in Pause. They include live tuning with units/reset, scenario tools, exact stepping, AI seats, debug overlays and validated version1 court editing/import/export. Developer-assisted runs are marked. Hub players have read-only diagnostics.\n\nSee REQUIREMENTS.md for implementation/evidence mapping, ../PROGRESS.md for checkpoints and issue history, and artifacts/verification.json and the suite JSON files for observed tests. Deliberate screenshots cover title focus, charged combat, collapse, repair/protection, phone framing, results and credits. Audio tests establish finite signals and bus isolation; sound quality is unknown without a listener.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"head -n 45 tests/view-browser.mjs && tail -n 20 tests/view-browser.mjs && cat > REQUIREMENTS.md <<'EOF'\n# Requirement and evidence ledger\n\nThe complete specification is in ../PLAN.md and ../TASK.md. These rows group related requirements without dropping their distinct acceptance paths.\n\n| Area | Implementation | Observed acceptance |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Native engine / packaging | Full 0.89.1 handoff, adapted artillery fixed-step/predictor design, native View/px/materials/props/Humanoid/Shell/ChipAudio; scripts/build.mjs | tests/artifact.mjs: exact released Hub bytes first, three inline scripts, no runtime asset URLs/absolute paths, metadata schema; exact final file tested |\n| Simultaneous charge | sim.js command state machine, capped power, fixed50° elevation, charge-time presets, stone lock, cancel/buffer/reload | simulation.mjs short/full holds, independent simultaneous releases, no unwanted buffer shots; ui-input.py human key/pad/touch cancellation |\n| Ballistics | Analytic per-step integration plus segment sweep; same production predictor; split at apex; explicit z-up boundary | Prediction/live agreement all stones both seats, thin-block sweep, all courts' exposed last fragments reachable, no NaN |\n| Objective destruction | Stable material blocks, authored directed support paths/foundations, atomic tick impacts and removal, visual debris | Real cascade without score farming, foundations persist, all5 AI courts finish, full tour collapses, browser actual duel demolition |\n| Tactical interruption | Crew retreat1.8s, launcher repair2.6s, endpoint max, input cancel, protected return1.25s, throw dedup | Both targets through real shots; overlap/protection/no queued shot fixtures; actual full tour both target kinds |\n| Scoring/outcomes | 3/7/13 direct score, winner × bout, loser0, mutual draw,90s normalized-health then score, frozen next actions | Unit ties/outcomes/exactly-once and full10 weighted total reconciliation; browser natural result/rematch |\n| Three stones | Round precision, masonry2.6 damage, deterministic3-way split, remembered range per type | All stone predictor/live runs and complete tour coverage, touch/keyboard/pad switching; native distinct art/audio |\n| Content / tour | Five different support layouts/moods, ten authored personalities, advance after loss, championship | Actual legal-command tour enters each court/bout, lesson shot+hit, losses advance, save clears at finish, replay begins1 |\n| AI | Common legal command interface; production trajectory search, support value, tactical protection at arrival; profile reaction/error | Deterministic all5-court completion; ordinary AI never writes hp/score; bounded search refinements for remnants |\n| Devices / TV | Native Shell menus, focus ring/hover, controller polling and explicit local seat assignments, last-device prompts, rebindable keys | ui-input.py two independent keys, two pads, disconnect pause, UI navigation, sliders; title/phone captures reviewed |\n| Touch / narrow display | Custom captured pointer holds, cancellation, contextual stone chips/halo; compact native side projection keeps whole lane | Physical client-space bounds regression, real CDP hold/release and chip tap, WebKit iPhone profile and pointercancel |\n| Settings / safety | Game-specific validated storage, three sound buses/mute, glyphs/tension/prediction/assist/reduced motion/UI scale, safe focus cancel | Corrupt/old/denied storage; settings retained; native START and unsupported-touch blocker regressions; gameplay never depends on audio |\n| Attract | Exact10s front-menu idle threshold, throwaway real bot world, all stones/courts, consumed exit | Exact before/at threshold assertions, shot state observed, no tour writes, keyboard/pad/touch exit coverage |\n| Developer | Pause workshop, scenario/AI seats/court/bout, restore/clear/result, pause/step/speed/invulnerability, collision/support/arc | UI navigation and tuning checks, fractional speed and exact step tests, cheated runs marked; hosted diagnostics read-only |\n| Court authoring | Version1 editable blocks, material/foundation/support fields, validation/import/export/apply/preview | Valid default roundtrip, malformed support/dimensions rejected, ballistic envelope and connectivity checked; UI author apply/export/import |\n| Code-only audio | Native synth custom instrument/patches plus formant gibberish, three buses, music.10 | Production offline music/effects/voice/mix nonzero finite, representative peak<1, all-bus mute0; acoustic quality unconfirmed |\n| Hub lifecycle | Active boot bypass, automatic ready, negative-clock wait, authoritative host incl no local seat, reliable intents/snapshots/ACKs, deadline/leave/end | Official harness normal/adverse150±50ms5%loss/host-leave/server cases; __hubCheck.pass and body complete; extra simultaneous firing match |\n| Hub fairness/traffic | Authenticated from->seat, seq/duration validation, bounded FIFO retry/cancel reserve, compact hp state, final ACK barrier | hub-unit.mjs duplicate/forgery/rejected-send/reorder tests; max snapshot and packet budget; both confirmed shots and silhouettes agree; no input/audio/messages after end |\n| Reports | metadata.json is sole source for game and root exit-interview.json | JSON parse/key/type/order checks, exact model/date/environment/usage, catalogue title/control/player consistency |\n\n## Refinements and justified implementation choices\n\n- Kept engine source unchanged. Custom game systems replace inherited walking, turn queue, angle adjustment, wind, rockets and inventory, following the plan.\n- Increased material health after initial native AI play ended in15–25s. The initial complete-tour driver then ran about14min of simulated bout time; subsequent tactical AI refinement favors castle targets for mason/broad personalities. A skilled bot is not a first-time human timing measurement.\n- Native Shell is retained, with custom simultaneous-seat routing so one confirm/fire cannot control both seats. Its touch controls are set off through native settings because the game supplies contact holds and a contextual stone selector.\n- Compact phone composition uses a public native custom View and320px buffer to avoid fixed-resolution minimum-scale cropping. Physics and collision are identical.\n- Local courts author editable block graphs rather than requiring full rigid-body settling. Unsupported blocks immediately leave objective/collision state and become finite cosmetic debris, as specified.\n- Hub uses periodic full compact dynamic state rather than fragile lossy block deltas. Static geometry regenerates from court/config; every passive client acknowledges reliable baselines. The host waits for final-state ACKs within supplied grace.\n- Standalone has same-device versus. Internet play is entered through AI Hub; no nonfunctional room browser is presented.\n- Validation uses documented stand-ins: no physical controller, touch hardware, TV, remote player, listener, or real iOS Safari was available.\nEOF\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Smithereen Royal Rumble\n\nOpen the HTML in the parent folder directly. It is self-contained and works offline. Hosted online play is entered by AI Hub; standalone supports solo and simultaneous same-device versus.\n\nHold **Space / left mouse / Cross** to wind. Release to throw. Watch the landing marker: full tension overshoots. **Q/E / L1/R1** changes stone; **C / right mouse / Circle** cancels. **Escape / Options** opens pause. Keyboard player two uses **Right Shift** and **U/O**. Touch holds in the friendly half and releases to throw; contextual arrows select stones. Controls can be rebound, glyphs changed to Xbox, and timing assistance enabled in Settings.\n\nA castle is the objective. Crew and launcher hits interrupt briefly, then return with visible protection. Unsupported sections collapse. A ten-bout tour advances after defeat and banks the winning direct score times the bout number. The last bouts carry more weight.\n\n\"'`npm ci` installs pinned build/test dependencies (no browser download needed on this workstation). `npm run build` deterministically publishes the exact single HTML and exit-interview.json to the parent folder, using metadata.json as the source for both credits and interview. `npm run verify` runs simulation, complete-tour, devices, artifact, production audio and official Hub harness checks, printing only failures and one count. Python Playwright uses the installed workstation venv; Node Playwright is pinned1.63.0 and uses the already installed browsers.\n\nDeveloper tools are available in Pause. They include live tuning with units/reset, scenario tools, exact stepping, AI seats, debug overlays and validated version1 court editing/import/export. Developer-assisted runs are marked. Hub players have read-only diagnostics.\n\nSee REQUIREMENTS.md for implementation/evidence mapping, ../PROGRESS.md for checkpoints and issue history, and artifacts/verification.json and the suite JSON files for observed tests. Deliberate screenshots cover title focus, charged combat, collapse, repair/protection, phone framing, results and credits. Audio tests establish finite signals and bus isolation; sound quality is unknown without a listener.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"import {chromium} from 'playwright';\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\nimport path from 'node:path';\nimport {fileURLToPath,pathToFileURL} from 'node:url';\nconst root=path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)),'..');\nconst project=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(root,'project.json'),'utf8'));\nexport async function runViewChecks({capture=false}={}){\n let count=0;const failures=[],report={};const check=(value,message)=>{count++;if(!value)failures.push(message);};\n const browser=await chromium.launch({headless:true});\n try{\n  const page=await browser.newPage({viewport:{width:1920,height:1080}}),errors=[];page.on('pageerror',e=>errors.push(e.message));\n  await page.goto(pathToFileURL(path.join(root,'..',project.basename+'.html')).href);await page.waitForFunction(()=>window.__rumble?.ui);\n  await page.evaluate(()=>{const a=window.__rumble;a.start('quick',{court:4,seed:21023});a.world.players[1].ai=null;});\n  await page.keyboard.down('Space');await page.waitForTimeout(980);\n  const charged=await page.evaluate(()=>{const a=window.__rumble;return{power:a.world.players[0].charge?.power,view:a.view.diagnostics(),errors:a.game.errors}});\n  check(charged.power>.3&&charged.power<1,'TV real keyboard hold must build visible tension');check(charged.view.prediction,'TV charge must generate a landing prediction');check(charged.errors.length===0,'Native TV view must draw without game errors');\n  if(capture)await page.screenshot({path:path.join(root,'artifacts/combat-tv-charged.png')});await page.keyboard.up('Space');\n  await page.waitForTimeout(700);check(await page.evaluate(()=>window.__rumble.world.stats.shots[0]===1),'TV keyboard release must launch exactly once');\n  const audio=await page.evaluate(async()=>{const a=window.__rumble;return{diag:a.audio.diagnostics(),mix:await a.audio.renderProbe(),music:await a.audio.renderProbe({music:1,effects:0,voice:0}),effects:await a.audio.renderProbe({music:0,effects:1,voice:0}),voice:await a.audio.renderProbe({music:0,effects:0,voice:1}),mute:await a.audio.renderProbe({music:0,effects:0,voice:0})}});\n  check(audio.diag.musicGain===.1,'Music default must be exactly 10%');check(audio.diag.context==='running','Audio must unlock on real keyboard gesture');\n  for(const [name,result]of Object.entries(audio)){if(name==='diag')continue;check(result.supported&&result.finite,`${name} offline audio must be finite`);if(name==='mute')check(result.peak===0,'Muted buses must render silence');else{check(result.nonzero,`${name} bus must render nonzero audio`);check(!result.clipped,`${name} representative audio must not clip`);}}\n  report.audio=audio;\n  await page.evaluate(()=>{const a=window.__rumble;a.world.players[1].crewUntil=a.world.time+1.7;a.world.players[1].launcherUntil=a.world.time+2.6;a.world.players[0].protectUntil=a.world.time+1.25;});await page.waitForTimeout(60);\n  if(capture)await page.screenshot({path:path.join(root,'artifacts/combat-tv-repair.png')});\n  await page.evaluate(()=>{const a=window.__rumble;for(const b of a.world.blocks)if(b.seat===1&&!b.foundation&&b.z<75){b.alive=false;b.hp=0;}a.world.revision++;});await page.waitForTimeout(180);\n  if(capture)await page.screenshot({path:path.join(root,'artifacts/combat-tv-debris.png')});\n  check(errors.length===0,'TV artifact must have no page errors');await page.close();\n  const context=await browser.newContext({viewport:{width:390,height:844},deviceScaleFactor:1,hasTouch:true,isMobile:true});const phone=await context.newPage();const phoneErrors=[];phone.on('pageerror',e=>phoneErrors.push(e.message));\n  await phone.goto(pathToFileURL(path.join(root,'..',project.basename+'.html')).href);await phone.waitForFunction(()=>window.__rumble?.ui);\n  await phone.evaluate(()=>{const a=window.__rumble;a.start('quick',{court:3,seed:21023});a.world.players[1].ai=null;a.device='touch';});await phone.waitForTimeout(100);\n  const phoneState=await phone.evaluate(()=>{const a=window.__rumble,s=a.game.screen,canvas=s.canvas,rect=canvas.getBoundingClientRect(),clientX=x=>rect.left+(x*s.S+s.OX)*rect.width/canvas.width;return{world:a.world.blocks.filter(b=>b.alive).map(b=>({left:clientX(a.game.view.ax*b.x-s.ix),right:clientX(a.game.view.ax*(b.x+b.w)-s.ix)})),W:a.game.W,H:a.game.H,OX:s.OX,chips:a.touchChips,errors:a.game.errors};});\n  check(phoneState.world.every(p=>p.left>=0&&p.right<=390),'Portrait phone must show both complete castle silhouettes in physical viewport');check(phoneState.OX>=0,'Portrait buffer must never be cropped by a negative letterbox offset');check(phoneState.chips.length===2,'Touch must expose contextual previous and next stone chips');check(phoneState.chips.every(c=>c.x>=0&&c.x+c.w<=390&&c.y>=0&&c.y+c.h<=844),'Phone stone chips must fit physical viewport');check(phoneState.errors.length===0,'Phone native view must draw without errors');\n  if(capture)await phone.screenshot({path:path.join(root,'artifacts/combat-phone.png')});\n  const chip=phoneState.chips.find(c=>c.delta===1);await phone.touchscreen.tap(chip.x+chip.w/2,chip.y+chip.h/2);await phone.waitForTimeout(40);check(await phone.evaluate(()=>window.__rumble.world.players[0].stone===1),'Touch contextual next stone must change the stone');\n  check(await phone.locator('[data-sys=need]:visible').count()===0,'Custom touch play must have no inherited controller-required blocker');\n  const cdp=await context.newCDPSession(phone);await cdp.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{type:'touchStart',touchPoints:[{x:95,y:635}]});await phone.waitForTimeout(700);\n  check(await phone.evaluate(()=>window.__rumble.world.players[0].charge?.power>.2),'A real held touchscreen contact must wind the launcher');\n  if(capture)await phone.screenshot({path:path.join(root,'artifacts/combat-phone-charged.png')});\n  await cdp.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{type:'touchEnd',touchPoints:[]});await phone.waitForTimeout(30);check(await phone.evaluate(()=>window.__rumble.world.stats.shots[0]===1),'Touch release must launch exactly once');\n  check(phoneErrors.length===0,'Phone artifact must have no page errors');await context.close();\n  report.charged=charged;report.phone=phoneState;\n }catch(e){failures.push(e.stack||String(e));}finally{await browser.close();}\n fs.writeFileSync(path.join(root,'artifacts/view-audio-evidence.json'),JSON.stringify({count,failures,report},null,2));return{count,failures};\n}\nif(process.argv[1]===fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)){const r=await runViewChecks({capture:process.argv.includes('--capture')});for(const failure of r.failures)console.error(failure);console.log(`${r.count} view/audio checks, ${r.failures.length} failures`);if(r.failures.length)process.exitCode=1;}\n  if(capture)await page.screenshot({path:path.join(root,'artifacts/combat-tv-debris.png')});\n  check(errors.length===0,'TV artifact must have no page errors');await page.close();\n  const context=await browser.newContext({viewport:{width:390,height:844},deviceScaleFactor:1,hasTouch:true,isMobile:true});const phone=await context.newPage();const phoneErrors=[];phone.on('pageerror',e=>phoneErrors.push(e.message));\n  await phone.goto(pathToFileURL(path.join(root,'..',project.basename+'.html')).href);await phone.waitForFunction(()=>window.__rumble?.ui);\n  await phone.evaluate(()=>{const a=window.__rumble;a.start('quick',{court:3,seed:21023});a.world.players[1].ai=null;a.device='touch';});await phone.waitForTimeout(100);\n  const phoneState=await phone.evaluate(()=>{const a=window.__rumble,s=a.game.screen,canvas=s.canvas,rect=canvas.getBoundingClientRect(),clientX=x=>rect.left+(x*s.S+s.OX)*rect.width/canvas.width;return{world:a.world.blocks.filter(b=>b.alive).map(b=>({left:clientX(a.game.view.ax*b.x-s.ix),right:clientX(a.game.view.ax*(b.x+b.w)-s.ix)})),W:a.game.W,H:a.game.H,OX:s.OX,chips:a.touchChips,errors:a.game.errors};});\n  check(phoneState.world.every(p=>p.left>=0&&p.right<=390),'Portrait phone must show both complete castle silhouettes in physical viewport');check(phoneState.OX>=0,'Portrait buffer must never be cropped by a negative letterbox offset');check(phoneState.chips.length===2,'Touch must expose contextual previous and next stone chips');check(phoneState.chips.every(c=>c.x>=0&&c.x+c.w<=390&&c.y>=0&&c.y+c.h<=844),'Phone stone chips must fit physical viewport');check(phoneState.errors.length===0,'Phone native view must draw without errors');\n  if(capture)await phone.screenshot({path:path.join(root,'artifacts/combat-phone.png')});\n  const chip=phoneState.chips.find(c=>c.delta===1);await phone.touchscreen.tap(chip.x+chip.w/2,chip.y+chip.h/2);await phone.waitForTimeout(40);check(await phone.evaluate(()=>window.__rumble.world.players[0].stone===1),'Touch contextual next stone must change the stone');\n  check(await phone.locator('[data-sys=need]:visible').count()===0,'Custom touch play must have no inherited controller-required blocker');\n  const cdp=await context.newCDPSession(phone);await cdp.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{type:'touchStart',touchPoints:[{x:95,y:635}]});await phone.waitForTimeout(700);\n  check(await phone.evaluate(()=>window.__rumble.world.players[0].charge?.power>.2),'A real held touchscreen contact must wind the launcher');\n  if(capture)await phone.screenshot({path:path.join(root,'artifacts/combat-phone-charged.png')});\n  await cdp.send('Input.dispatchTouchEvent',{type:'touchEnd',touchPoints:[]});await phone.waitForTimeout(30);check(await phone.evaluate(()=>window.__rumble.world.stats.shots[0]===1),'Touch release must launch exactly once');\n  check(phoneErrors.length===0,'Phone artifact must have no page errors');await context.close();\n  report.charged=charged;report.phone=phoneState;\n }catch(e){failures.push(e.stack||String(e));}finally{await browser.close();}\n fs.writeFileSync(path.join(root,'artifacts/view-audio-evidence.json'),JSON.stringify({count,failures,report},null,2));return{count,failures};\n}\nif(process.argv[1]===fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)){const r=await runViewChecks({capture:process.argv.includes('--capture')});for(const failure of r.failures)console.error(failure);console.log(`${r.count} view/audio checks, ${r.failures.length} failures`);if(r.failures.length)process.exitCode=1;}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
