,\\\"fix\\\":\\\"Use public touch off setting instead of refusing touch\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"view-browser and WebKit unsupported-overlay absence plus real touch Fire\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":6,\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Live slider rebuilt its DOM during pointer drag\\\",\\\"fix\\\":\\\"Apply live value without replacing control until change finishes\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"UI input range interaction and health-fraction/reset checks\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":7,\\\"severity\\\":\\\"critical\\\",\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Network pending-begin latch survived crew interruption and blocked future Fire\\\",\\\"fix\\\":\\\"Retire begin when authoritative charge/hold/buffer cleared\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"hub-unit real production crew interruption: two regression failures before fix, zero after\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":8,\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Lesson replay could replace saved solo tour and practice could retain score ledger\\\",\\\"fix\\\":\\\"Independent quick teaching mode, clear active tour outside war modes, preserve saved tour\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"simulation practice-result and saved-tour separation regressions\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":9,\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"issue\\\":\\\"Long credits auto-focus scrolled source heading offscreen\\\",\\\"fix\\\":\\\"Paged controller-readable credits and stable heading visibility\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Focused Credits viewport regression and final-credits screenshot\\\"}\n]\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"agent_message","text":"The integrated verification run completed 406 checks. Its only failure was a test comparing an audio gain to exact decimal equality; Web Audio returned the expected tiny float difference, so I’ve corrected the assertion. Visual review also found poor credits scrolling, which is being replaced with short controller-readable pages before the final run.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,pathlib\np=pathlib.Path('metadata.json');m=json.loads(p.read_text())\nm['testingFeedback']=[\n'9 distinct player-facing issues were found and fixed: TV title clipping, overlapping native touch START, prestart Hub pause, cropped portrait battlefield, an introduced unsupported-touch blocker, interrupted slider dragging, post-interruption online Fire lockout, saved-tour pollution by lesson practice, and credits heading scrolling. The issue ledger records fixes and regression evidence.',\n'3 were game-breaking: portrait cropping made remote targets unusable, the unsupported-touch overlay blocked touch-only play, and the stale network begin latch blocked subsequent Fire after recovery. All have regression checks.',\n'The complete legal-command ten-bout driver verified integrated gameplay and weighted totals; the extra two-player Fire/recovery test caught problems official conformance alone missed, and physical phone-coordinate assertions exposed cropping.',\n'The initial headless draw-only pass was least helpful for device layout: it produced no renderer errors while the physical phone viewport was still cropped. Screenshot inspection and client-space bounds were necessary.'\n]\nm['engineFeedback'][1]='I initially guessed Hub meta names and used touch:never to hide native touch controls. The released contract required session-specific meta names, and touch:never means unsupported touch. Reading the actual APIs led to the correct declarations and native touch=off with custom gestures.'\nm['sourceInformation']['testing']='Actual automated Node simulation, complete ten-bout legal-command tour, all five courts, native headless draws, browser UI/device and production offline-audio checks; Playwright1.63.0 Chromium, WebKit iPhone profile and Firefox Canvas; controller stubs and real emulated touch; official Hub normal,150ms latency±50ms jitter/5%loss, host-leave, dedicated-server and active Fire cases. No physical controller, touch hardware, real iOS Safari, TV, remote human or listener; acoustic quality unknown.'\np.write_text(json.dumps(m,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nPY\ncat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Final refinement checkpoint\n- Initial integrated npm run verify: **406 checks**, one failed assertion due to Web Audio float32 gain .10000000149 being compared with exact decimal .1. Changed assertion to tight tolerance; no audio defect.\n- Updated online recovery regression now **39/39** (was35): a real crew hit cleared production charge but left the network begin latch; this blocked fresh Fire after recovery. Fixed retirement and observed the regression fail twice before the fix, pass after.\n- Added practice/tour separation and replay-preserves-save regressions; teaching now requires a real castle impact, not a temporary crew hit. AI profiles favor intended tactics; error slider scales profile error and timing changes lock to the next action.\n- Final full-tour evidence before natural-loss variant:718.24 simulated bout seconds (~12min), all10bouts/all5courts, actual demolition in8bouts plus2timeouts, all3stones,93crew/162launcher interruptions,80cascade block removals. This is a skilled test driver, not an ordinary-human timing estimate.\n- Added natural passive-player loss in bout4 to explicitly verify advance after defeat. Added exact attract threshold, prior menu/focus restoration, and an~86s two-court showcase with real40s deadline/ceremony segments.\n- Phone target inset now uses actual remaining objective blocks, magnifies the last fragment, and preserves the complete lane. View diagnostics/test assertions added; final captures pending.\n- Credits visual review found source heading scrolled offscreen by focus on bottom actions. UI agent implementing short readable pages and visibility regression.\n- Metadata now documents9 distinct observed player-facing issues,3 critical, actual tests and limits, engine wrong guesses, and prompt feedback. Complete issue list: development artifacts/issues.json.\n- All final reports derive from metadata.json. Pending: final build + full verification, inspect final inset/credits captures, publish/report exact count.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
