{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_94","type":"agent_message","text":"Built **[Smithereen Royal Rumble](./Smithereen-Royal-Rumble-Stone-Sling-Smithereens-1980-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-033000.html)**. Open the HTML directly to play offline.\n\n[Exit interview](./exit-interview.json) · [Progress and evidence](./PROGRESS.md)\n\n**Source Information:** Date: 2026-11-06 03:30:00. Source label: Stone Sling Smithereens - 1980. Plan: PLAN.md. Genre: simultaneous artillery action/strategy/sports; fixed side-on 2D. Tech: JavaScript, my-3D2dge 0.89.1, Hub client 1.4.0, esbuild 0.25.12. Original native pixel art, Humanoid rigs and animated machinery; code-only music, effects and gibberish voices, with music at 10%. Includes solo, local versus and hosted Hub versus. Research used the [official manual](https://odyssey2.info/library/manuals/us_smithereens/smithereens.txt) and engine/Hub contracts. Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux. Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort ultra. Usage: **added on import**.\n\n**Testing Feedback:** **449 checks passed, zero failures.** Fixed 11 player-facing issues, including 3 critical issues. Full-tour and network-recovery tests were most helpful; initial headless drawing missed phone cropping. Physical hardware and acoustic quality remain unconfirmed.\n\n**Engine Feedback:** Native rendering and headless simulation worked well. Initial touch-mode and Hub-metadata guesses needed correction. Combat, structural collapse and network authority were custom-built; lifecycle integration was hardest. Engine source stayed unchanged. A documented multiplayer artillery adapter would help.\n\n**Prompt Feedback:** Delivery requirements and testing stand-ins were clear. The historical source year was ambiguous. Integrating complete gameplay across devices and networking was hardest. A machine-readable acceptance checklist would improve the prompt."}}
